  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hi,\n\nI would like to request a native implemented feature for floating / flying for vrchat. Currently, for non FBT users (meaning \"Half Body\" and Desktop) the only real way of achieving that is to use some locomotion / collider setup, which lifts the avatar into the air.\n\nI think (especially smaller) avatars would benefit hugely from such a feature.\n\nSince it would open a lot of more freeroaming capabilities, limitations must most likely be made as well. For that having an option to enable/disable flight/float per world (for example over the website, like I can enable/disable world debugging there) might already do the trick. \n\nFor the locomotion part, having a value like \"flying\" set to true when one enters flight/float would be awesome as well, so we locomotion creators can properly work with flight as well.\n\nAlternatively, if completely flying is off the charts, having the ability to lift yourself up (like +2/+4 Y in world space) to float would already be a huge boon, so that huge differences in avatar height can be mitigated. For that again the example, that a 1.70m avatar will have issues seeing my 0.35m one when both are standing, me able to float up to their eyeheight would be hugely beneficial.\n\nbest\n\nGireison",
